      <h2 class="section-h2">Open source at 1.0, your data, and one thing I have not picked.</h2>
      <div class="lic three">
        <div class="lic-cell">
          <p class="k">License</p>
          <p class="v">MIT, at 1.0.</p>
          <p class="body">The source goes public with 1.0, under MIT like the Loadout skills: the app, the Workers behind Coach and Social, and the command-line tools it grew out of. Then read it, change it, ship your own. The Ironstack name and the marks stay with Mission Built.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lic-cell">
          <p class="k">Price</p>
          <p class="v">Not settled yet. Here is why.</p>
          <p class="body">Every Coach question runs on a server I pay for. I want Coach in the app and I am not willing to lose money keeping it there, so the launch price is open: free with Coach on an allowance, a one-time price, or Coach as the paid part of a free app. What is settled: logging, the clock, your whole history and Social will not be what you pay for.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lic-cell">
          <p class="k">Your data</p>
          <p class="v">On your phone. Yours to take.</p>
          <p class="body">Your log is files on your phone, and one tap exports all of it in the Mission Built Schema, a format documented in public. Coach and Social send only what they need to work. One screen deletes everything, everywhere, and tells you what it deleted. <a class="inline-link" href="/rack/ironstack/privacy">The privacy page</a> says exactly what, where and for how long.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fine">
        <p class="k">Not a doctor. Not your programmer.</p>
        <p>I am not a coach or a clinician, and nothing on this page or in the app is advice about how you should train. Ironstack is how I log my own. Coach is an AI: it gives a starting weight under a ceiling it can show you, a cue from your own notes, or an alternative when the rack is taken. It will not write your program, and any question about pain or injury gets pointed to a qualified person.</p>
